{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unmystical-grassgreen-iggypops","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Documentation + portability: mapping seam, provider-neutral reuse, migration safety\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nThe mapping seam (S1–S8) adds a new config surface, new echo-safe behaviors (breadcrumb,\nreplay), and a new probe command. Operators and future integrators need authoritative docs,\nand the plan-review `project.portability` criterion requires that no capability's only\ntrigger is a specific CI provider — the seam must work across environments with diverse or\nno CI. This child closes the documentation and portability story: it documents the seam end\nto end, records the provider-neutral reuse contract for future Linear/GitLab/GitHub-Issues\nintegrations, and states the migration/rollback story (the feature is additive — an absent\n`[tool.rebar.mapping]` section reproduces today's hardcoded behavior exactly).\n\n## Approach\n\nAuthor docs across the surfaces the seam touches:\n- `docs/config.md` — the `[tool.rebar.mapping]` reserved section reference (extends S1's\n  leaf doc): full axis catalog, the three-layer merge, per-project keying, fail-closed\n  validation, and the orthogonality to `.bridge_state/projects.json`.\n- A mapping-seam guide (new `docs/mapping-seam.md`, indexed in `docs/README.md`) covering\n  the provider-neutral core vs Jira-adapter split, the capability descriptor, the\n  skip/drift/collapse decision paths, transition replay, the parent breadcrumb, and the\n  probe workflow — with the explicit statement that the neutral core is the reuse seam for\n  future targets (Linear/GitLab/GitHub-Issues) whose direct support is out of scope now.\n- `CHANGELOG`/migration note — additive, backward-compatible: absent section = current\n  behavior; no store migration; rollback = delete the section.\n- Portability statement: every mapping behavior is exercised by in-process unit tests with\n  injected transports (no live Jira, no specific CI required); the only live touchpoint\n  (the probe) degrades to an offline emit and is never a CI gate.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `docs/config.md`, `docs/mapping-seam.md` (new), `docs/README.md` (index entry).\n- A migration/rollback note in the repo's changelog surface.\n- No source-code change (docs-only child) — file-impact is the doc paths.\n\n## Testing\n\nDocs-only child: no automated test tier. Verification is by review against the acceptance\ncriteria (the plan-review gate defers testing on a docs child to a reviewer-checkable\noutcome). The portability *claim* it documents is substantiated by the unit suites in\nS1–S8 (each names an injected-transport, no-live-Jira tier); this child asserts those exist\nand are referenced, it does not add new behavior to test.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/config.md` documents the full `[tool.rebar.mapping]` axis catalog, merge\n  layers, and per-project keying — verified by reviewer check that each axis (status, type,\n  link, priority, create_defaults) and the merge order appear.\n- [ ] `docs/mapping-seam.md` exists, is indexed in `docs/README.md`, and states the\n  provider-neutral core as the reuse seam for future targets — verified by reviewer check\n  for the index entry and the reuse statement.\n- [ ] The migration note states the feature is additive with an absent-section = current-\n  behavior guarantee and a delete-the-section rollback — verified by reviewer check.\n- [ ] The portability statement records that every mapping behavior is covered by\n  injected-transport unit tests requiring no live Jira and no specific CI provider —\n  verified by reviewer check against the S1–S8 test sections.\n\nTest tier: **none (docs-only)** — the mechanism is documentation; the observable oracle is\nreviewer verification against the four criteria above, which is the correct tier for a\nchild that adds no runtime behavior.","id":"14f4-d616-70df-466d","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Documentation + portability: mapping seam, provider-neutral reuse, migration safety"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787290338813130001,"uuid":"af718ae8-d361-4af6-b40d-26a93eee3f3e"}